import AFTD.Prelude
import AFTD.Kb.Tcs.SimpleGraphLeapGroup

/-!
# simple_graph_is_leap_closed

Topic: graphs   Node: d10252887a30

Provenance: formalization of a published result. Source: arXiv:2610.18463 Question 5.9: The group generated by a graph's derangements

An edge subset F of a simple graph G is leap-closed (leap-maximal) if F is a subset of the edge set of G and for every edge e in E(G) \ F, the leap group of the spanning subgraph with edges F ∪ {e} strictly contains the leap group of the spanning subgraph with edges F.
-/

/-- An edge subset of a simple graph is leap-closed (leap-maximal) if adding any edge strictly enlarges its leap group. -/
def simple_graph_is_leap_closed {V : Type*} (G : SimpleGraph V) (F : Set (Sym2 V)) : Prop :=
  F ⊆ G.edgeSet ∧
  ∀ e ∈ G.edgeSet \ F,
    simple_graph_leap_group (SimpleGraph.fromEdgeSet F) <
    simple_graph_leap_group (SimpleGraph.fromEdgeSet (insert e F))
